Re-run this whenever ce-pg changes. It is idempotent: a doc with the same title under
the same parent is UPDATED, not duplicated.

WORKSPACE-LOCAL ON PURPOSE. It hardcodes the ids of one Ocean workspace, which is
exactly the kind of thing that must never live inside a repo that travels. The repo's
own README and skill stay canonical; these pages are the human-facing mirror.

Copy this shape to document another app. Two things Ocean's dialect will teach you the
hard way: there are NO TABLES (a table line becomes one paragraph blob), and
`md.render` emits the doc title as the page heading, so a body that opens with its own
`# Title` renders it twice.
"""
