Every serious app eventually wants relational storage, and the usual answer is a page
of instructions: install postgres, initdb, pick a port, create a role, invent a
password, put it in an env var, remember to migrate. Each app repeats it, each machine
does it slightly differently, and the credentials end up in as many places as there are
