discovered by name, authorized by a signed attenuating chain, scoped per database, and
reachable from whichever node needs it. `ce-pg` is that door.

## The one call an app needs

```python
pg = Postgres(ce.connect().wait_ready())
db = pg.ensure("myapp", migrations_dir="migrations")   # idempotent: run it every boot

db.exec("insert into notes(body) values ($1)", ["hello"])
rows = db.rows("select id, body from notes order by id desc limit $1", [10])
```

