## Conventions it keeps

- **Discovery by service name**, never a stored `ip:port`; it re-resolves once on any
  transport failure.
- **Degrade, never error-box.** The last known state stays on screen, marked "cached,
  reconnecting", while it retries with capped backoff. An empty screen saying "failed to
  fetch" is the defect — see [[App anatomy — State / Logic / Viz, docs, robustness]].
- **Unauthorized is not failure.** `status` is open and `db.list` needs `pg:admin`, so
  the two are fetched independently: a viewer without the capability sees the cluster and
  a line naming the grant it would need, rather than an error.
- **A read op must never do work.** Tables and migrations are fetched only when you
  expand a row, never for every database on load.
- **Self-contained.** No imports, no build step, styles in the shadow root. The module
  file IS the artifact and its sha256 is its content address in the manifest.

Parent: [[ce-pg — postgres as a capability of the mesh]]
"""
